It only does the work for your current set.  It doesn't tell you what
_can_ happen.
Consider an orcish barbarian: say you find a spellbook of magic
mapping, is it worth it to keep the book so that one day it can be
used?  Only if one plans on being greater than level 14 with INT=3D21
and wearing a robe.  At level 15 the failure rate is 96%, dropping to
a still sad 74% for a level 30.  In other words, forget the spell
unless you plan on playing an endurance game.
In my current game I found a spellbook of identify.  With a robe at
level 14 and with int=3D16 casting identify has an 88% failure rate.  So
depending on how many scrolls of identify I find, I might keep the
robe stashed in my bag for closet-casting.  But only maybe ...


